                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_312">Lichfield,
                        Staffordshire. Cathedral church of St Mary the Virgin and St Chad</orgName><p>Rawlinson A.389 belonged to two prebendaries of Lichfield in s.
                        xv ex. At end: 'Liber magistri Thome Rynold' and 'Liber Magistri Iohannis
                        Redhill'; both were prebendaries of Lichfield in s. xv2.</p><p>No. 73 in
                        Patrick Young's catatlogue of the Lichfield cathedral manuscripts, 1622--3.
                        </p><p>The flyleaf, fol. iii, is from a 13th-cent. MS of Isidore of
                        Seville's Etymologiae.</p><p>Mark of chain (?) shows at foot of fols. iii
                        recto and i recto.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Young
